Root Cause
Cloud Run deployment runs the Node.js package.json lifecycle (npm run build and npm start), which failed because package.json and a runnable entrypoint were missing after cleanup (and previously pointed to a non-existent server.ts / vite build).
Android Lint also flagged two minSdk 24 compatibility errors in LinuxTerminalEngine (Process.waitFor(timeout) and Process.destroyForcibly() require API 26+).
Fixes Applied
Added Zero-Dependency Cloud Run Entrypoint (package.json & server.js):
Uses Node.js 22 built-ins only (node:http, node:fs, node:path) with clean build, dev, start, and lint scripts.
Automatically binds to DEFAULT_APP_PORT (3000) inside the local preview container and PORT (8080) in deployed Cloud Run containers.
Serves GET /health (200 OK), GET / (the EdgeCode APK preview page), and GET /app-debug.apk when the APK artifact is present.
Fixed Android Lint API-24 Compatibility: Guarded Process.waitFor(timeout) and Process.destroyForcibly() with Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.O and added an API 24 polling/destroy fallback.
